    "finding": "SCALE MISMATCH, not a weighting choice. compute_citation_score log-normalises citations to a full [0,1] range, while BGE cosine similarities within a top-100 pool span only ~0.087. At the documented 0.7/0.3 weights the citation term therefore drives ~5x more ranking variance than relevance: the formula is nominally 70/30 relevance-first but behaves as ~83/17 citation-first. At 0.8/0.2 it is still ~2.9x. Fix = min-max normalise the dense score within the fetched pool before combining, so both terms span [0,1].",
